                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a really awesome idea. It is similar to a 1v1 MOBA, except the VR player is a god. The VR player is then able to control a hero and join the troops on the field and fight against the PC player. Sounds awesome in concept. I have enjoyed playing it with my friends, however it is pretty bare bones and leaves a bit to be desired at the moment. It is an early access game, so that is to be expected.\n\n[h1]PC: [/h1]The controls and fighting style of the PC player are slightly clunky and difficult at times. All around just not very smooth. [i]Yet[/i]. Fingers crossed. And while the flying is a nice touch, and levels the playing field a bit, the animations of it are slightly comical. The flight controls are acceptable.\n\n[h1]VR: [/h1]As the VR player the bow mechanics leave a lot to be desired currently. The melee combat coupled with the movement (which is done via the trackpad) is not that effective or enjoyable. It seems to put a hastily made FOV blocker to reduce motion sickness. It works, but it's just a picture with a little hole in the middle, instead of the usual fading black. It was also kind of weird to see under it. But it served it's purpose.  I hope that all of this changes with updates, as it easily could become my favorite local multiplayer game. \n\n[h1]tldr;[/h1] I'm going to recommend this game, mainly because I like the concept, I did have fun, and I want to see this game succeed and develope into something amazing. However, if you are expecting a fully fleshed out, local multiplayer game to spend hours upon hours playing with friends, you may want to wait a bit to jump on this one. \n\nCurrently: 6.5/10",
